From: d4r
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: fingerprint the loaded ZLUDA DLL in the module cache key

On Linux the module cache key includes libcuda.so's size and modification time, so a rebuilt ZLUDA never
reuses modules compiled by an earlier build with the same git revision (patch 0002). The Windows build
returned no fingerprint and keyed the cache on the git revision alone: after rebuilding ZLUDA with a
different d4r patch set, the cache in %LOCALAPPDATA%\zluda kept serving the old compiles. Use the size and
modification time of the loaded nvcuda.dll there too.
---
diff --git a/zluda/src/impl/module.rs b/zluda/src/impl/module.rs
index 9f72f2f..5d7e734 100644
--- a/zluda/src/impl/module.rs
+++ b/zluda/src/impl/module.rs
@@ -467,9 +467,23 @@ fn loaded_library_fingerprint() -> Option<String> {
     ))
 }
 
+// d4r: as on Linux, the cache key includes this DLL's size and modification time, so a rebuilt ZLUDA
+// (another patch set at the same git revision) never reuses modules an earlier build compiled.
 #[cfg(windows)]
 fn loaded_library_fingerprint() -> Option<String> {
-    None
+    let path = zluda_windows::get_module_path_for_function(zluda_build_version as usize)?;
+    let metadata = fs::metadata(path).ok()?;
+    let modified = metadata
+        .modified()
+        .ok()?
+        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)
+        .ok()?;
+    Some(format!(
+        "{:x}.{:x}.{:x}",
+        metadata.len(),
+        modified.as_secs(),
+        modified.subsec_nanos()
+    ))
 }
 
 fn get_cache_key<'a, 'b>(
